r.", "Calibration and fixture are confounded: the untuned session does not record its fixture, the two tuned sessions used different fixtures. Within a session the comparison is clean; between untuned and tuned it is trim and fixture together.", "The printed figure pools the two tuned sessions and both repetition rates, as this page does by default. Splitting the sessions shows how far each alone places the null; pooling moves it most at 20 ns.", "12 tables are counted twice in the printed figure: under 'Manual edit of waveform markers' (24 Sep, 25 V), the 19-30 ns tables carry exactly their parents' values. Six 20 ns tables from a '0.1ms coupledMeasurements' folder sit under the 1 ms folder and are tagged 1 ms although their names say 0.1 ms. Neither moves the 100 or 50 ns nulls by more than 0.1 V; at 20 ns the pooled tuned null is 133.6 V as printed, 152.0 V without the copies and 131.2 V without either. All lie beyond 80 V. Both are toggles here.", "The deliverable band (up to 80 V) is the figure's own shading, not a measured limit."]}
